{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Building locally","modules":[{"name":"OpenUSD"}]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to use SwiftUsd with local\/existing OpenUSD binaries"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/buildinglocally"]},{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftusd\/buildinglocally"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/BuildingLocally","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUsd comes with pre-built OpenUSD binaries that make it easy to start using SwiftUsd without additional setup. To do so, follow the instructions in "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" to add SwiftUsd as a remote package dependency to an Xcode project or Swift Package. However, if you want to use SwiftUsd with different Usd feature flags or on other platforms\/architectures, you can build OpenUSD to your specifications, and then create a Swift Package that lets you use your OpenUSD build in Swift."}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Clone SwiftUsd","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"zsh","code":["git clone git@github.com:apple\/SwiftUsd.git ~\/SwiftUsd"]},{"type":"orderedList","start":2,"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Clone OpenUSD v26.05","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"zsh","code":["git clone https:\/\/github.com\/PixarAnimationStudios\/OpenUSD.git ~\/SwiftUsd\/openusd-source","cd ~\/SwiftUsd\/openusd-source","git checkout v26.05"]},{"